title: Docker Installation
description: Run FOSSBilling with Docker for a consistent, isolated environment.
sidebar:
  label: Docker Installation
  order: 4
---

## Prerequisites

- [Docker Engine](https://docs.docker.com/engine/install/) installed on your system

## Choose a Setup

{% aside %}
Use the `latest` tag for the current stable release.
{% /aside %}

{% aside type="caution" title="Keep the Installer Private" %}
The examples below bind the container's HTTP port to `127.0.0.1` only. Do not expose the installer directly over HTTP: it receives database and administrator credentials. For remote or production use, configure and verify a TLS-terminating reverse proxy before opening the installer.
{% /aside %}

{% tabs %}
{% tabitem label="Standalone" %}
The simplest option. This runs only the FOSSBilling container, so you must provide your own database service.

```bash
docker run -d \
  --name fossbilling \
  -p 127.0.0.1:8080:80 \
  -v fossbilling:/var/www/html \
  --restart unless-stopped \
  fossbilling/fossbilling:latest
```
{% /tabitem %}
{% tabitem label="Docker Compose" %}
This option brings up FOSSBilling and MariaDB together, which makes it the fastest way to get started.

```yaml {% meta="title='docker-compose.yml'" %}
services:
  fossbilling:
    image: fossbilling/fossbilling:latest
    restart: unless-stopped
    ports:
      - "127.0.0.1:8080:80"
    volumes:
      - fossbilling:/var/www/html
    depends_on:
      - mariadb

  mariadb:
    image: mariadb:lts
    restart: unless-stopped
    environment:
      MARIADB_DATABASE: fossbilling
      MARIADB_USER: fossbilling
      MARIADB_PASSWORD: ${MARIADB_PASSWORD:?set-a-strong-database-password}
      MARIADB_RANDOM_ROOT_PASSWORD: "1"
    volumes:
      - mariadb:/var/lib/mysql

volumes:
  fossbilling:
  mariadb:
```

For a new installation, create a `.env` file beside `docker-compose.yml`. Replace the placeholder with a strong database password and keep the file private.

```dotenv {% meta="title='.env'" %}
MARIADB_PASSWORD='replace-with-a-strong-password'
```

Start the stack from that directory. Compose reads `.env` automatically.

```bash
docker compose up -d
```

The first startup downloads container images and may take a few minutes. Keep the same `MARIADB_PASSWORD` when starting the stack again with the existing database volume.

**Database credentials** (if using the example above):
- Hostname: `mariadb`
- Database: `fossbilling`
- Username: `fossbilling`
- Password: the value of `MARIADB_PASSWORD` in `.env`
{% /tabitem %}
{% /tabs %}

## Complete the Installer

If your browser runs on the Docker host, open `http://localhost:8080` to continue with the installer. This HTTP endpoint is intended only for local setup on the Docker host.

For remote or production use, configure a TLS-terminating reverse proxy that forwards `X-Forwarded-For`, `X-Forwarded-Host`, and `X-Forwarded-Proto: https`, then enable trusted-proxy support when prompted and complete the installer using its HTTPS URL, such as `https://billing.example.com` (see [reverse-proxy setup](/getting-started/installation/#pre-installation-steps)). Do not replace the loopback mapping with a public port and enter installer credentials over remote HTTP.

## Post-Installation

The official Docker image runs FOSSBilling cron automatically every five minutes inside the container.

You do not need to add a host crontab entry when using the official Docker image.

See [Docker Updates](/maintenance/updating/#docker-updates) when updating FOSSBilling or replacing its container image.
